=== 9/10/2026
	Revising all updates made to PyramydOS and creating a changelog starting from version 0.0.0 (Initial commit)

- Initial Commit (98a6997), 2/10/2026, Version 0.0.0, Began project, features implemented:
	- Console
	- GDT
	- IDT
	- PMM
	- VMM
	- Allocator (growing-heap)
	- ACPI
	- HPET
- Merge pull request #1 from adambassem256-crypto/feature/apic (5f15d8a), 4/10/2026, Version 0.1.0
- APIC timer, and minor changes (31f24a4), 6/10/2026, Version 0.2.0
- Fixed license (AGAIN) (e658d2f), 6/10/2026, Version 0.2.1
- Updated README (d6a611f), 6/10/2026, Version 0.2.2


=== 9/10/2026 - Version 0.3.0
	Added random numbers, UUID and UUID generator, and some string functions (2e1d19a)

- Added Changelog
- Removed project structure from README because I'm too lazy to update it everytime I add an update :)
- Updated README (added buttons)
- Updated License to have the new username (adambassem256-crypto -> adam-bassem)

Latest version: Version 0.3.0

=== 12/10/2026 - Version 0.4.0
	Removed flanterm, added custom terminal emulator and renderer

=== 17/10/2026 - Version 0.5.0
    Added PCIe, updated GDT(*)

(*) -> Created set_rsp0 function to set kernel stack, in preparation to adding scheduler and syscalls

=== 21/10/2026 - Version 0.5.1
    Clean up code, remove architecture abstraction

--- Notes
- Removed "#if defined(__x86_64__)" since I'm not planning on supporting any other architecture
- Cleaned up some stuff
- Replaced #define with constexpr
- Made APIC timer fire at 10hz frequency instead of the old 1000hz
- Minor change in ACPI (check if reported RSDP table length is smaller than struct size)
- Added some comments
